    "title": "Read books and Daily Devotionals",
    "path": "4 Discover Watch Reels sermons live Library Daily Devotional and COT AI > Read books and Daily Devotionals",
    "content": "Open Library from General COT Home when it appears among the three visible shortcuts, or choose View more, then Library under COT. Search by book title or author, choose a cover to open the reader, and use Continue reading to resume saved EPUB progress when signed in.\nEPUB books: Choose a chapter and use Previous or Next to move through page-like sections. When the source contains them, the reader separates the heading, Scripture, Memory Verse, devotional body, and Prayer / Reflection into clear sections. Repeated chapter or date headings, page labels, and decorative lines are removed from the spoken text. Choose Read aloud, select 0.5×, 0.75×, 1×, 1.25×, 1.5×, or 2× Voice speed, or choose Stop. COT saves signed-in reading progress automatically.\nPDF books: PDFs open in a dedicated full-screen reader and keep their original page layout. Use the header Back control to return to the book. Use Previous and Next, enter a page number to jump, and use the zoom controls. If the PDF provides bookmarks, choose a Document Sections item to jump to that section. Choose Read aloud to hear text from the current page, choose Auto read to continue page by page, choose 0.5×, 0.75×, 1×, 1.25×, 1.5×, or 2× Voice speed, or choose Stop. COT speaks long pages in consecutive parts and cleans page numbers, decorative fragments, and split words when the PDF's extractable text permits. Changing the page or Voice speed stops the current speech; start again at the new page or speed. A scanned image-only PDF may need optical character recognition (OCR). Open original PDF appears only when the embedded reader cannot display the file.\nReviews: Signed-in members can choose one to five stars, add an optional review of up to 2,000 characters, and choose Post review. Posting again updates that member's review for the book.\nDaily Devotional: Open it from a General COT Home shortcut, choose View more and then Daily Devotional, or use the card at the top of Library. Use the date navigator to choose the previous or next day, open Devotional date and select a day from the calendar, or choose Today. The calendar supports dates from 2000 through 2200, and Today follows the date on your device. A published reading can show its title, Scripture, Memory Verse, devotional message, and Prayer / Reflection as distinct sections. Choose Listen, select 0.5×, 0.75×, 1×, 1.25×, 1.5×, or 2× Voice speed, or choose Stop.\nNo reading for a date: Choose another day. Ministry publishers can add the missing entry or map dated chapters from an attached devotional EPUB.",
    "sourceDocumentId": "1tzW_4eU9yDzKHGjey4dxcUbMRPnRyThP-TtY0B2dD2M",
